The main improvement ,I believe,
would be to use the number of ways to make a specific pattern
instead of appending the pattern and checking for duplicates
If number of ways to make n is f(n), then
Example: Number of ways to make 4 would be
    = f(1) * f(3) + f(2) * f(2) + f(3) * f(1)
    It might be clear that the first and last terms are identical
    It shouldn't be double counted.
